{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"safety_classification\", \"batch_id\": \"safety_batch_08\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_93b55bb025f2663a\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_93b55bb025f2663a/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"Prompt-injection claims vs actual output content\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_72f38361c53cc0d7a8104488\", \"member_7ca50d66cfaf19a7eed3cb59\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks which category applies when an output pretends to ignore policies.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790889905.000065\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790889905.000065\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor asks whether roleplay jailbreak wording is automatically unsafe and how to handle the task.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911054.000066\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U011\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911054.000066\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"In the QA tutor's thread, the team lead instructs participants to separate prompt-injection language from actual output content before choosing a safety category and asks whether there are harmful instructions or merely an override boast.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890002.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890002.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890002.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"In the tutor's thread, the team lead instructs participants to separate prompt-injection language from actual output content before choosing a safety category.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911193.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911193.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U011\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911193.000339\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that the model boasts about ignoring safeguards but gives no procedural details in the thread started by a different tutor.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911101.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911101.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U011\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911101.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current project FAQ directs inspection of what the output actually does, distinguishing a boast alone from harmful instructions or actionable bypass content; the classification guide says boasting about ignoring rules without corresponding harmful content does not alone establish a violation or QN trigger.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:1300a08e\", \"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:3008b16b\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT\", \"text\": \"The team lead's current batch announcement requests task references for uncertain labeling of jailbreak-like outputs and says there is no final decision yet; its directive concerns collecting examples, not a new classification rule.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790924776.000064:406e00de\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790924776.000064:406e00de\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The supplied member threads record a handling approach but no specific task category, and no reply supplies the content distinction requested by the team lead in the QA tutor's thread.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790889905.000065\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790889960.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890002.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911054.000066\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911101.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911148.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911193.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890002.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890002.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor and a tutor ask how to classify outputs that claim to ignore policies or use roleplay jailbreak wording.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790889905.000065\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911054.000066\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790889905.000065\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U011\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911054.000066\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"The team lead has answered the handling approach in both threads: separate prompt-injection language from actual output content before choosing a category; specific task categories remain unrecorded.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890002.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911193.000339\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790889905.000065\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790889960.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911054.000066\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911101.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911148.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890002.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890002.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911193.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U011\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911193.000339\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"In the tutor's thread, a different tutor reports that the model boasts about ignoring safeguards but gives no procedural details.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911101.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911101.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U011\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911101.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"In the QA tutor's thread, the team lead asks whether the output contains harmful instructions or merely an override boast; the supplied thread contains no answer to that request.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890002.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790889905.000065\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790889960.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911054.000066\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911101.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911148.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911193.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890002.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890002.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d3\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The current FAQ and classification guide distinguish a boast alone from actual harmful instructions or actionable bypass content.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:1300a08e\", \"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:3008b16b\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d4\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The batch announcement asks for task references for uncertain jailbreak-like outputs and records no final decision; it does not establish a new classification rule.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790924776.000064:406e00de\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790924776.000064:406e00de\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:no_action\", \"kind\": \"NO_ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why no further action is needed now: The team lead already answered the handling approach in both threads, and those answers agree with current guidance. The remaining task-specific content check does not establish a need for a new policy intervention.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890002.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911193.000339\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:1300a08e\", \"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:3008b16b\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790889905.000065\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790889960.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911054.000066\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911101.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911148.000226\", \"k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790924776.000064:406e00de\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"announcement:k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790924776.000064:406e00de\", \"kind\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING\", \"text\": \"This announcement applies to this topic and directs current handling: \\\"Share a task reference if you see this; no final decision yet.\\\". The announcement concerns the same batch and uncertainty about jailbreak-like outputs. It directs sharing task references for example collection, not a classification change or escalation route.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790924776.000064:406e00de\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_72f38361c53cc0d7a8104488\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_72f38361c53cc0d7a8104488 is PARTIALLY_RESOLVED: The team lead gives the QA tutor a handling approach but requests a content distinction that receives no answer in the supplied thread; no specific category is recorded.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790889905.000065\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790889960.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890002.000226\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_7ca50d66cfaf19a7eed3cb59\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_7ca50d66cfaf19a7eed3cb59 is PARTIALLY_RESOLVED: The team lead answers the tutor's handling question by distinguishing prompt-injection language from output content, but the supplied thread records no final task category.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911054.000066\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911101.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911148.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911193.000339\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity LOW: The questions concern a distinction already explained in current guidance and answered by the team lead in both threads. The member messages do not report incorrect submitted labels, blocked work, or conflicting handling instructions.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790889905.000065\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911054.000066\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911101.000113\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790889905.000065\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_72f38361c53cc0d7a8104488\", \"thread_id\": \"1790889905.000065\", \"author_id\": \"U002\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T21:25:05.000065Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U002\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Output pretends to ignore policies — category?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790889960.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_72f38361c53cc0d7a8104488\", \"thread_id\": \"1790889905.000065\", \"author_id\": \"U014\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T21:26:00.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U002\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Are we classifying an attempted override prompt or the actual model output? We should inspect the actual response content instead of trusting its self-description.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890002.000226\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_72f38361c53cc0d7a8104488\", \"thread_id\": \"1790889905.000065\", \"author_id\": \"U006\", \"author_role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T21:26:42.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U002\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"We need to separate the prompt-injection language from the actual output content before choosing a safety category. Is there harmful instruction content here, or merely a boast about an override?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"THREAD_SCOPE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911054.000066\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_7ca50d66cfaf19a7eed3cb59\", \"thread_id\": \"1790911054.000066\", \"author_id\": \"U011\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T03:17:34.000066Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U011\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"[Task review]\\nIssue: Is roleplay jailbreak wording automatically unsafe?\\nQuestion: what is the correct handling for this task?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911101.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_7ca50d66cfaf19a7eed3cb59\", \"thread_id\": \"1790911054.000066\", \"author_id\": \"U010\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T03:18:21.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U011\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"The model boasts about ignoring safeguards but gives no procedural details.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911148.000226\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_7ca50d66cfaf19a7eed3cb59\", \"thread_id\": \"1790911054.000066\", \"author_id\": \"U008\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T03:19:08.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U011\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"What harmful content, if any, is present beyond a claim of bypassing a rule?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911193.000339\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_7ca50d66cfaf19a7eed3cb59\", \"thread_id\": \"1790911054.000066\", \"author_id\": \"U006\", \"author_role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T03:19:53.000339Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U011\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"We need to separate the prompt-injection language from the actual output content before choosing a safety category.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"THREAD_SCOPE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:4a0a4f89\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"safety-classification-instructions@1.4\", \"title\": \"Safety Classification — Instructions (v1.4)\", \"sections\": [\"Tool incidents and submission\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"safety-classification-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-10T15:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-10T15:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"safety_classification\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Tool incidents and submission\\nIf the response does not load, report a response-fetch incident and leave content classification unassessed. Do not invent a safety label for unseen output.\\n\\nFor submission failures, capture task ID, field state and error. Selecting a category is not confirmation that submission completed. Assess operational impact separately from content categories.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:1300a08e\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"safety-classification-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Safety Classification — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Context and labels\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"safety-classification-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-12T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-12T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"safety_classification\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_